---
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import "../styles/product.css";

const title = "Getting started — Machine Control";
const description =
  "Install Machine Control on your computer or VM, choose permissions, and connect your AI agent. Find setup guides for physical iPhones, Chromebooks, and other devices.";
const agentPrompt = `Use the installed Machine Control app to help me with <task> on <target>.

Find its bundled control CLI and read its agent instructions. If discovery
is unclear, use https://machinecontrol.dev/getting-started/ and the linked
installed-CLI guide. Inspect target readiness and available capabilities.

Use only the scopes I authorize. Request approval when needed, respect Pause
and Stop, and obtain control-session ownership where the platform requires it.
Prefer native UI and browser controls, with screenshots and input as needed.
Verify the observed result of your actions and report any uncertainty.

For a configured VM, run the read-only doctor and acquire an exclusive claim
before meaningful use. Renew it while working and release it during cleanup.
For physical devices, follow their setup, exact selection, and lease rules.
Use outer console input only for explicitly authorized bootstrap or recovery.`;
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/getting-started/">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="product-page product-start">
    <section class="page-intro start-intro">
      <div class="shell start-shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Computer or VM · Mac, Windows &amp; Linux</p>
        <h1>Install the app. Connect your agent.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Start with Machine Control on the computer you want to use. The desktop
          app includes the control CLI and its Python runtime, so your agent can
          use it without cloning the repository or installing Python separately.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/downloads/">Download Machine Control</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="#agent-prompt">Copy the agent prompt ↓</a>
        </div>
        <p class="product-scope-note">Need to create or prepare a VM first?
          Start with the <a href="/virtual-machines/">VM toolbox and setup guides</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="first-session">
      <div class="shell start-shell">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Your first desktop session</p>
          <h2>Four steps to useful control.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="product-setup-steps">
          <li>
            <span>01</span>
            <div><h3>Install and open Machine Control</h3>
              <p>Choose the download for your operating system and architecture.
                Install on your physical computer or inside the VM you want to
                control. The app runs in the menu bar or tray.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>02</span>
            <div><h3>Follow Permissions</h3>
              <p>On Mac, enable Accessibility and Screen Recording. On Linux,
                approve GNOME screen/input sharing when needed. For browser
                control, follow Chrome extension setup in the app.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>03</span>
            <div><h3>Point your agent to the bundled CLI</h3>
              <p>Give an agent that can run commands the prompt below. It can read
                the CLI's agent instructions and discover your installed control
                surface. <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/blob/main/topics/installed-agent-cli.md#contract">Installed CLI locations and discovery</a></p></div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>04</span>
            <div><h3>Choose access, then start the task</h3>
              <p>Enable selected scopes and duration in Access, or approve a
                native request. Turn access off whenever you need to. On Mac and
                Windows, Pause and Resume let you temporarily stop control.
                Review activity in the app.</p></div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="product-scope-note">Desktop grants normally apply to callers
          running as your user. They do not contain an agent with an unrestricted
          same-user shell. <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/blob/main/desktop/README.md#approval-and-control-boundaries">Read the access boundaries</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-ink" id="agent-prompt">
      <div class="shell start-shell">
        <div class="prompt-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Your choice of agent</p>
            <h2>Give your agent a task and a target.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Replace the two placeholders. Use your computer, a configured VM,
            or a prepared physical device as the target.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="agent-prompt-card">
          <div class="agent-prompt-toolbar">
            <span>Machine Control handoff</span>
            <button type="button" data-copy-prompt aria-describedby="copy-status">Copy prompt</button>
          </div>
          <pre data-agent-prompt><code>{agentPrompt}</code></pre>
          <p id="copy-status" class="copy-status" data-copy-status aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-white" id="devices">
      <div class="shell start-shell">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Physical devices and remote computers</p>
          <h2>Prepare the device you want to reach.</h2>
          <p>iPhone and Chromebook control have their own setup. These routes use
            native device tools and the common CLI, rather than a desktop
            installer on the device.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="product-device-grid">
          <article class="product-card">
            <h3>Physical iPhone</h3>
            <p>Prepare an authorized Mac, pair the device, enable Developer Mode,
              and provision the signed XCTest runner. Device trust and protected
              authentication keep their native requirements.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/tree/main/platforms/ios">iPhone setup guide →</a>
          </article>
          <article class="product-card">
            <h3>Chromebook</h3>
            <p>Use a dedicated developer-mode Chromebook and follow its bootstrap
              guide for native desktop, browser, capture, and input access.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/tree/main/platforms/chromeos">Chromebook setup guide →</a>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="product-card-links product-guide-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/tree/main/platforms/android">Android</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/tree/main/platforms/quest">Quest</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/tree/main/platforms/steamdeck">Steam Deck</a>
          <a href="/virtual-machines/">VM creation and coordination</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/blob/main/docs/target-registry.md">Target configuration</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="advanced">
      <div class="shell start-shell product-advanced">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Optional capabilities</p>
          <h2>Go further when you need it.</h2>
          <p>Locked-screen access on Mac and Windows requires explicit opt-in,
            helper preparation, and supported platform conditions. Use the
            <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/blob/main/platforms/macos/docs/locked-use.md">Mac guide</a>
            or <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/blob/main/desktop/WINDOWS-LOCKED-USE.md">Windows guide</a>
            before enabling it.</p>
        </div>
        <p>For source checkouts, headless use, scripts, claims, and isolated VM
          workspaces, follow the <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/blob/main/docs/cli-guide.md">CLI guide</a>.
          Linux dependencies and installation details are in the
          <a href="https://github.com/kzahel/machine-control/blob/main/desktop/LINUX.md">Linux guide</a>.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/downloads/">Download the app</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/#targets">Explore devices</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>

<script>
  const copyButton = document.querySelector("[data-copy-prompt]");
  const promptElement = document.querySelector("[data-agent-prompt]");
  const copyStatus = document.querySelector("[data-copy-status]");

  if (copyButton instanceof HTMLButtonElement && promptElement instanceof HTMLElement) {
    copyButton.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(promptElement.textContent ?? "");
        copyButton.textContent = "Copied";
        if (copyStatus) copyStatus.textContent = "Prompt copied to the clipboard.";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          copyButton.textContent = "Copy prompt";
          if (copyStatus) copyStatus.textContent = "";
        }, 2400);
      } catch {
        if (copyStatus) copyStatus.textContent = "Select the prompt text and copy it manually.";
      }
    });
  }
</script>
